Z||000014||Patrick's Dad||12-24-2001||11:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B> For starters, perhaps we should reconsider subsidizing children through tax breaks</B> <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First of all, I (we) didn't decide to have children because of the tax writeoff. It costs far more to raise a child than I'll ever <I>pay</I> in taxes.<P>You obviously don't have them, and, with that attitude, I'd advise you to keep it that way, before we read about you in the newspaper.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> <B>and further tightening up welfare resrtrictions and limitations.</B> <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Although I agree with this in principle,it is for other reasons. Most welfare recipients can't afford two and three cars.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> <B>Maybe even compell those of us who do have children to pay a higher share of public education.</B> <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I already pay enough, and my children aren't using the public schools, So I pay another $4K for my son (my daughter isn't two yet.) to go to a good school.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> <B>Offer reduced or free birth control, vasectomies, and whatever they call having a woman's tubes tied.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you, perchance, rayb?<P>Let's encourage more sex for more disease and other problems. Let's not teach self control and responsibility. We've dealt with this before.<P>What we need is more roads with fewer obstructions to accomodate the cars that we are free to buy and drive, not curbs on our rights to freely go to work or assemble wherever the heck we feel like. And some of us (like my city girl wife) should learn to appreciate the clean air and lack of light pollution that rural America offers.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||12-24-2001||12:30 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B> think all would be ok if...<BR> 1. All women driver's stay at home!!!  unless they are driving a Fiero.. wheeww...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> 2. All the car's that are made oversea's would stay off of the road.. just during daylight hour's... <BR> 3. All people over the age of 60 only drive on Sunday's....<BR> 4. and....  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1. be glad there aren't more females on the forum, I bet they'd take offense to the first comment..........<BR>2. Hmm, Porsches are made overseas.. yet Civics are made here....<BR>3. agree, sorta.. not all people over 60 are bad drivers or drive slow, my boss is 60 and he had a 5spd Camaro until a couple of years ago.. but there are a lot of really bad old drivers, I was almost in several accidents with the same old lady last summer, just drove right thru a stop sign, I had to slam on the brakes.. she didn't even slow down when she went by, just about brushed my front bumper.. another time that month, she was driving down the middle of the road, with cars parked on both sides.. I had nowhere to go, so I had to swerve in and out of 2 empty parking spots to get by.. once again, she didn't even slow down or look at me. I know who she is, she lives about 2 blocks away from me, and used to babysit my sister and I when we were young. that doesn't change the fact that she's a dangerous driver.<P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000016||fierospeeder||12-25-2001||10:23 AM||||sex education isn't going to solve the over population.<P>Theres the people that want a "big family", even if they cant afford it.  Those kids grow up, and own a car when their 16, then they get their own homes.  More land is needed for the new homes that have to be built on.<P>A lot of these "moms" cant even handle 3 kids, and they want more.   Just talk to a woman how kids are everything.  And after the kids mature and are in grade school, the moms are too tired to be with the kids.<P><BR>Thats one cause of too many people on the road.  Another are these people that have nothing better to do with their day.  Like going to the grocery store to buy toothpicks in their SUV.  A lot of these useless trips.  And its like senior citizen day every day, so they are going to the zoo to get their discounts.<P>Suvs on the road, dont help a bit.  They are longer and take up more space.  If people bought ricers instead of SUVs.<P>exponentialy we will be overtaken with too many cars and people.  Im wondering how long it will take until all our farmland and forrests will gone||||reg||1
Z||000017||BN Boomer||12-25-2001||12:17 PM||||Patrick's dad, calm down and stop being such a presumptuous a$$. No, I'm not rayb. I am somewhere near the opposite end of the political spectrum from him.<P>I do have kids. 3 of them. My oldest daughter is about to start college. I never said people have kids specifically for the tax deductions, did I? I just think that removing the current tax incentives for children would give some folks cause to more seriously consider how many they have or having them in the first place.<P>My reply, and I believe this thread in general, are not simply to deal with congested roads, but rather overpopulation. What are we going to do when our country has as many people per square mile as New York? Build more roads? How that approach been taken or worked for New York?<P>Regarding various forms of birth control, my insurance will pay for the high expense of multiple pregnancies and deliveries, but won't pay for a simple vasectomy. Sounds kind of stupid, doesn't? Or should I just use self control and responsibility and not have sex with my <B>WIFE</B>?<P>Trying thinking outside of the box for a change.||||reg||1
